{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The SanDisk microSD card feels useful because I have repeatedly bought memory cards, along with a reader and storage cases; a spare fits that ongoing use.",
    "Including an adapter matches my history of buying cards and accessories that help me use storage across compatible devices."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The older Fire tablet duplicates the newer Fire 7 I already have with a fitted case, rather than helping me do something new.",
    "The streaming sticks do not address a current need, and the 4K version adds little for my listed 720p TV.",
    "Smart speakers and a smart plug introduce voice-control uses I have not shown interest in; buying power strips does not mean I want home automation.",
    "The HDMI cable is a practical accessory, but I have no identified connection that needs a ten-foot cable."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "Owning a Fire tablet seems to have been taken as interest in a broader collection of Alexa devices.",
    "My electronics purchases seem to have been interpreted as interest in entertainment gadgets generally, although most purchases serve specific accessory needs."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My repeated purchases of memory cards, a reader, and storage cases show a continuing storage need more clearly than a desire for another main device.",
    "My latest lens-cap purchase and earlier tripod purchases suggest that useful camera accessories still matter to me.",
    "What I already own matters: an accessory should fit an existing device or solve a concrete problem, while another tablet may simply duplicate my setup."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The memory card fits my recurring accessory needs, but most suggestions mistake device ownership for a desire to expand into streaming and voice control."
}"}
